<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῐθ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for stones</i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
					3.128
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; but usu. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθικά</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλία</span>),
				τά, <i>a treatise upon precious
			stones</i>, title of Orphic poem, ap.<i><span class="en">
				Tz.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ λίθων</span> codd.); also
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλία λιθιακά</span> Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				<u>Prooem.</u>
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιθικά</span>, of <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
			</span></i>'s work, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.323
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for stone</i> in the bladder, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.60
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
